# Traffic System — Mobile Platform for South African Traffic & Licensing Services

## Project Overview
A secure, user-friendly mobile platform that digitizes South African traffic and licensing services. The app aims to reduce queues, save citizens time, improve accessibility, and provide a central place for traffic-related services and information.

## Problems & Proposed Solutions
1. Long queues at traffic departments
   - Problem: Citizens spend hours waiting; many leave without being assisted.
   - Solution: Online bookings and appointments, digital access to services, reduced branch visits.

2. No central mobile platform
   - Problem: Information is scattered across systems.
   - Solution: One mobile app with a centralized dashboard for all traffic services.

3. Forgotten driver's licenses
   - Problem: Drivers sometimes leave physical licenses at home.
   - Solution: Secure Electronic Driver's License with QR/NFC verification and biometric identity confirmation.

4. Unclear license collection status
   - Problem: Citizens don't know when cards are ready; repeated trips.
   - Solution: Real-time status tracking, collection notifications (email & in-app).

5. Difficulty booking appointments
   - Problem: Limited visibility of available slots.
   - Solution: Appointment booking system showing branch schedules, available slots and times.

6. Traffic fine management
   - Problem: Drivers unaware of outstanding fines or camera tickets.
   - Solution: Fine-tracking dashboard with details and in-app payments.

7. Vehicle license renewal challenges
   - Problem: Forgotten renewal dates lead to penalties.
   - Solution: Renewal reminders, online license disk payments, expiry notifications.

8. Poor communication from traffic departments
   - Problem: Citizens miss important updates.
   - Solution: Push notifications, email alerts, collection reminders, department announcements.

9. Limited access to traffic information
   - Problem: Drivers unaware of closures, accidents, congestion.
   - Solution: Real-time traffic updates, road-closure alerts, alternative routes and travel estimates.

10. Accessibility challenges
   - Problem: Some users struggle due to disabilities.
   - Solution: AI chatbot assistance, voice-friendly support, accessible navigation.

11. Lack of digital learning resources
   - Problem: Learner drivers have limited prep materials.
   - Solution: Learner's license lessons, practice tests, and booking for learner tests.

12. Data and connectivity limitations
   - Problem: Users may lack mobile data or have intermittent connectivity.
   - Solution: Offline mode, low-data design and cached critical documents.

13. Cashless and convenient payments
   - Problem: Citizens may not have cash; payment processes are inconvenient.
   - Solution: Cardless payments, instant EFT, mobile payments and secure transactions.

## Main Project Goal
Create a secure, reliable mobile platform that centralizes South African traffic and licensing services, reduces in-branch queues, improves accessibility, and gives citizens timely, convenient digital access to licensing, fines, appointments, and real-time traffic information.

---

## Recommended App Structure & Navigation
Bottom navigation (primary):
- Home — Dashboard showing license/vehicle status, fines, appointments, collection status, expiry alerts, recent notifications, traffic alerts, weather summary, and quick actions (Pay Fine, Renew License Disk, Book Appointment, View Digital License, Report Issue).
- My Licenses — Driver's license (digital), QR/NFC verification, license number, expiry, renewal status; vehicle licenses and disk expiry, ownership and collection status.
- Services — Appointment booking, renewals, learner & driver tests, change of ownership, vehicle registration, document uploads, and applications.
- Payments — Fine payments, payment history, license disk payments, registration fees, receipts and multiple payment methods (card, instant EFT, mobile wallets).
- Traffic & News — Real-time traffic, closures, accidents, congestion, suggested routes, travel-time estimates, weather, and department announcements.

Top-right: Profile menu (not a bottom tab)
- Profile contains personal information, linked vehicles and licenses, security settings (Face ID, Fingerprint), email & notification settings, language & accessibility settings, help center (chatbot), and logout.

## User Flow (Login -> Home)
1. User enters South African ID number (or phone/email)
2. Firebase Authentication
3. Find user document and retrieve userId
4. Fetch user-related collections:
   - users, driversLicenses, vehicles, fines, appointments, notifications
5. Display consolidated Home screen with status and quick actions

---

## Recommended Firestore Structure
Use a clear collection layout to keep data normalized and performant.

Collections (core):
```
users
 └── {userId}
      ├── idNumber
      ├── fullName
      ├── email
      ├── phone
      ├── province
      └── createdAt

driversLicenses
 └── {licenseId}
      ├── userId
      ├── licenseNumber
      ├── issueDate
      ├── expiryDate
      ├── status
      └── qrCode

vehicles
 └── {vehicleId}
      ├── ownerId
      ├── registrationNumber
      ├── make
      ├── model
      ├── year
      └── diskExpiry

fines
 └── {fineId}
      ├── userId
      ├── vehicleId
      ├── amount
      ├── offense
      ├── status
      └── issuedDate

appointments
 └── {appointmentId}
      ├── userId
      ├── serviceType
      ├── branch
      ├── date
      ├── time
      └── status

payments
 └── {paymentId}
      ├── userId
      ├── amount
      ├── paymentType
      ├── status
      └── paidAt

notifications
 └── {notificationId}
      ├── userId
      ├── title
      ├── message
      ├── read
      └── createdAt

branches
 └── {branchId}
      ├── name
      ├── address
      ├── province
      ├── phone
      └── operatingHours

roadAlerts
 └── {alertId}
      ├── title
      ├── location
      ├── severity
      ├── description
      └── createdAt

news
 └── {newsId}
      ├── title
      ├── content
      ├── image
      └── publishedAt
```

Optional/Advanced collections:
- learnerTests — practice questions and test data
- supportChats — chatbot conversation logs and user support threads

For a final-year project, the 10 core collections above are sufficient to implement the main features while keeping the database manageable and production-like.

---

## Authentication & Login Flow (detailed)
- User provides SA ID number (or registers via phone/email)
- Use Firebase Auth to verify identity (OTP/email link)
- On success, query Firestore for the user's document, then load related collections for the dashboard
- Secure sensitive features (digital license access, payments) with biometric or MFA confirmation

## Implementation Notes & Recommendations
- Prioritize data security and encryption for personal documents (IDs, licenses).
- Use offline-first strategies and caching for critical documents and last-known statuses.
- Design for low-data usage and provide an optional "lite" mode for limited connectivity.
- Implement push notifications and email alerts for license collection, renewals, fines, and appointments.
- Provide clear accessibility settings and voice/AI chatbot support for users with disabilities.

